  .sidebar { display:none; }
  ...
}
```
But hiding upgrades on landscape means no gameplay progression. Could allow sidebar scroll? Hmm. Maybe keep scene and let page scroll; users can rotate portrait. Mobile games often support portrait. The game is clearly portrait-first. Not a blocker.

Maybe add a "rotate to portrait" hint? Overkill.

At tablets (e.g., 768x1024), media 940 layout stacks; scene 58vh=594; topbar 62+11 etc; sidebar below. It's scrollable, fine.

