content.text:
Now visibility pause for patience. Current bindEvents:
```
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", () => {
      if (document.hidden) saveState();
    });
```
Replace with hiddenAt logic. On hidden: hiddenAt = Date.now(); saveState(); On visible: if hiddenAt, shift expiresAt and nextOrderAt by delta, hiddenAt=0. Also maybe lastFrame = performance.now() to avoid huge dt (dt clamped to 0.2 anyway). Add.

```
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", () => {
      if (document.hidden) {
        hiddenAt = Date.now();
        saveState();
        return;
      }
      if (hiddenAt) {
        const pausedFor = Math.max(0, Date.now() - hiddenAt);
        hiddenAt = 0;
        state.orders.forEach((order) => { order.expiresAt += pausedFor; });
        state.nextOrderAt += pausedFor;
        lastFrame = performance.now();
      }
    });
```
Note state.nextOrderAt may be 0/NaN? It's numeric. Fine.

Edit.

